Station T-19, located in Survey Area T, presents a four-layer subsurface model. The sequence features a significant resistive increase from layer 1 (609.2 $\Omega\cdot$m) to layer 2 (7309.9 $\Omega\cdot$m), followed by a decrease in layer 3 (4367.7 $\Omega\cdot$m) and a subsequent slight increase in layer 4 (4556.7 $\Omega\cdot$m). 

Based on these resistivity transitions, the first triplet (layers 1-2-3) follows a K-type pattern (low-high-low) and the second triplet (layers 2-3-4) follows an H-type pattern (high-low-high). The resulting curve type is KH, which is consistent with the classification currently on file.

